.TH "FLOX\-SERVICES\-STOP" "1" "" "" "Flox User Manuals"
.SH NAME
flox\-services\-stop \- stop running services
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
flox [<general\-options>] services stop
     [\-d=<path> | \-r=<owner/name>]
     [<name>] ...
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Stops the specified running services.
.PP
If no services are specified, then all services will be stopped.
If any of the specified services are not currently running, a warning
will be displayed and the remaining services will be stopped.
.PP
If any of the specified services do not exist, an error will be returned
and no services will be stopped.
If an error is encountered while stopping one of the specified services,
the remaining services will still be stopped, but a warning will be
displayed for the services that failed to stop, and a non\-zero exit
code will be returned.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[CR]<name>\f[R]
The name(s) of the services to stop.
.SS Environment Options
If no environment is specified for an environment command, the
environment in the current directory or the active environment that was
last activated is used.
.TP
\f[CR]\-d\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-dir\f[R]
Path containing a .flox/ directory.
.TP
\f[CR]\-r\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-reference\f[R]
A FloxHub environment, specified in the form \f[CR]<owner>/<name>\f[R].
.TP
\f[CR]\-D\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-default\f[R]
Use your default environment (\f[CR]<your\-user>/default\f[R]).
When unauthenticated in an interactive context, you will be prompted to
log in.
In non\-interactive contexts (e.g., scripts or CI), this flag will fail
with an error when authentication is missing.
.SS General Options
.TP
\f[CR]\-h\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-help\f[R]
Prints help information.
.PP
The following options can be passed when running any \f[CR]flox\f[R]
subcommand but must be specified \f[I]before\f[R] the subcommand.
.TP
\f[CR]\-v\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-verbose\f[R]
Increase logging verbosity.
Invoke multiple times for increasing detail.
.TP
\f[CR]\-q\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-quiet\f[R]
Silence logs except for errors.
.SH EXAMPLES
Stop a running service named `server':
.IP
.EX
flox services stop server
.EE
.PP
Stop all running services:
.IP
.EX
flox services stop
.EE
.PP
Attempt to stop a service that doesn\(cqt exist:
.IP
.EX
$ flox services stop myservice doesnt_exist
✘ ERROR: Service \(aqdoesnt_exist\(aq not found.
.EE
.PP
Attempt to stop a service that isn\(cqt running:
.IP
.EX
$ flox services stop running not_running
⚠️  Service \(aqnot_running\(aq is not running
✔ Service \(aqrunning\(aq stopped
.EE
